# agent-harness:project-gitignore:v1:start
# Managed block. Its source is .agents/templates/gitignore in the harness repository; edit it
# there and re-run EnsureProject. Anything you add outside these markers is preserved.

# Task-hook runtime state. hook-state.js writes <repo-root>/taskstate/<project-id>/ by its own
# design -- session-local records, allow-tag usage among them -- which belong to one device and
# one session rather than to the project. It was never ignored, so every project running the
# hooks accumulated an untracked directory in its root that a `git add -A` would commit.
taskstate/

# The pre-relocation location for the same state. A session that predates the move still writes
# here, so a project can acquire this directory without any current tool creating it.
.claude/state/

# The codex dispatch marker. auto-schedule-codex-poll.js writes it into <repo-root>/.claude/ on
# PostToolUse for a codex subagent, and its own body tells the session to delete it once the
# wakeup is scheduled -- so a session that ends before that leaves it behind. Named rather than
# ignoring `.claude/`, which is a real product configuration directory a project may track.
.claude/codex-dispatch-pending.json

# Linked worktrees kept inside the repository. A worktree's own files are tracked by ITS checkout,
# never by this one, so an unignored .worktrees/ shows as untracked here and a `git add -A` would
# commit a second copy of the tree. The convention is one place per repository: agent worktrees go
# in .worktrees/<task>, product-managed ones stay wherever their product puts them. On 2026-08-14
# nine agent-harness worktrees were spread across four roots, two of them siblings of the project
# in Projects\, where they read as separate projects.
.worktrees/

# Work Scope transaction scratch. State and evidence writes go to a temp file beside the target and
# are renamed into place, so a write killed mid-transaction -- a hook timeout, an interrupted
# session, a closed laptop -- leaves the temp behind. Nothing sweeps them: `Reconcile-WorkState
# -Repair` reports the state valid and drift-free while the leftovers stay on disk. Measured
# 2026-08-15 in this repository: six of them untracked, which a `git add -A` would have committed.
.agents/work/tmp/
.agents/work/**/*.tmp

# Compiled-assembly cache for WorkScope.psm1's two C# blocks. The module used to re-run the C#
# compiler on every import -- 742 ms of a ~900 ms import, measured 2026-08-15 under pwsh 7.6.4,
# paid by every process the task hooks start. It now compiles once to a DLL beside itself, keyed
# by a hash of the source and the runtime version. Build output, never source: it is rebuilt on
# demand, differs per machine and per pwsh version, and a committed copy would be loaded as code
# on someone else's machine.
.agents/tools/.assembly-cache/
# agent-harness:project-gitignore:v1:end

# Copyrighted source material — NEVER commit (personal/local use only)
content-private/
book.json
*.pdf

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
node_modules/
.vercel
.local/
.worktrees/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.superpowers/sdd/2026-08-22-total-money-makeover-full-fidelity/task-4-independent-pdf-audit.json

# Project task state is tracked for cross-agent handoffs.
